course: dictionary
lesson: 4432
title: Names with a capital letter
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A name of a particular person, place or thing is a proper noun, and it starts with a capital letter. «Handel» is a name, so it begins with a capital H. That capital letter is your first clue that it is not an ordinary word.
explain: The example sentence says «composers such as Bach, Handel and Vivaldi wrote music for it». Bach, Handel and Vivaldi are names of composers, people who write music. Here Handel is the family name of one composer.
explain: Look at the words around a name to find out who or what it means. The sentence tells you Handel wrote music, so the clue is the word composers. You can check by asking: is this the name of a person, a place or a thing?
fact: A proper noun is the name of a particular person, place or thing, and it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Handel is a name: George Frideric Handel (1685–1759) was a German-born composer who lived and worked in London.
fact: Handel wrote «Messiah», «Water Music» and «Music for the Royal Fireworks».
fact: Handel can also be a surname, the family name of a person.
fact: Handel is not an English common word, so do not confuse it with handle.
exercise: In «composers such as Bach, Handel and Vivaldi wrote music for it», what kind of word is Handel? | *A proper noun, the name of a composer | An adjective for a sound | A common noun for a thing | A verb for holding something
exercise: Which of these is the name of a composer who lived and worked in London? | Water Music | Messiah | Recorder | *Handel
exercise: Why does Handel start with a capital letter? | Because it names a common thing you can hold | *Because it is the name of a particular person | Because it is the first word of every sentence | Because it is a very long word
test: Which piece did Handel write? | Peter Pan | *Music for the Royal Fireworks | Swan Lake | Hamlet
test: Handel is a name. Which common English word should you NOT confuse it with? | Hand | *Handle | Candle | Handsome
exam: In «The recorder is a real instrument: composers such as Bach, Handel and Vivaldi wrote music for it», which word is a proper noun naming a composer? | recorder | instrument | music | *Handel
